sentences.t:
ingentemque Gyas ingenti mole Chimaeram,
urbis opus, triplici pubes quam Dardana versu
impellunt, terno consurgunt ordine remi;

sentences.l:
and the huge, Gyas, of huge bulk, Chimaera,
a city's work, which in triple row the Dardan youth
drive on; in threefold tier rise the oars;

sentences.t:
Est procul in pelago saxum spumantia contra
litora, quod tumidis submersum tunditur olim
fluctibus, hiberni condunt ubi sidera cori;

sentences.l:
There is far out in the sea a rock, the foaming opposite
shores, which by the swollen, submerged, is beaten at times
waves, when the wintry hide the stars north-westers;

sentences.t:
Huc dirige gressum;
litus ama, et laevas stringat sine palmula cautes;
altum alii teneant.

sentences.l:
Hither direct the step;
the shore love, and the left let graze, allow, the oar-blade, rocks;
the deep let others keep.”

sentences.t:
“Nunc, nunc insurgite remis,
Hectorei socii, Troiae quos sorte suprema
delegi comites;

sentences.l:
“Now, now rise up to the oars,
Hectorean comrades, whom of Troy in the lot last
I chose as companions;
